Compare channel layouts with av_channel_layout_compare().

_audio_ch_layout_differs() compares AVChannelLayout.u.mask directly.  That
union member only holds the channel bitmask when .order is
AV_CHANNEL_ORDER_NATIVE or AV_CHANNEL_ORDER_AMBISONIC; for
AV_CHANNEL_ORDER_CUSTOM the very same bytes are the

    AVChannelCustom *map

pointer (libavutil/channel_layout.h: union { uint64_t mask; AVChannelCustom
*map; } u).  On a custom-ordered layout the test therefore compares two heap
addresses as if they were masks -- it is not a crash, the union read is
defined, but the verdict is meaningless.

The result decides whether "channel_layouts=" is added to the aformat filter
and whether asetpts is inserted at all (_audio_requires_asetpts), so a wrong
verdict silently drops a needed conversion or adds a pointless one.

av_channel_layout_compare() dispatches on .order and handles every case,
including comparing a custom layout against an equivalent native one.

Reported upstream against PR #2117.

--- src/transcoding/transcode/audio.c.orig
+++ src/transcoding/transcode/audio.c
@@ -104,12 +104,13 @@ _audio_encoder_frame_size(TVHContext *self)
 static int
 _audio_ch_layout_differs(TVHContext *self)
 {
-    if (self->iavctx->ch_layout.nb_channels != self->oavctx->ch_layout.nb_channels)
-        return 1;
-    if (self->iavctx->ch_layout.nb_channels &&
-        self->iavctx->ch_layout.u.mask != self->oavctx->ch_layout.u.mask)
-        return 1;
-    return 0;
+    /* u.mask is only the channel bitmask for AV_CHANNEL_ORDER_NATIVE and
+       AV_CHANNEL_ORDER_AMBISONIC.  For AV_CHANNEL_ORDER_CUSTOM the same union
+       member is the AVChannelCustom *map pointer, so comparing u.mask there
+       compares two pointer values as if they were masks.  Let libavutil decide
+       instead: av_channel_layout_compare() dispatches on the order. */
+    return av_channel_layout_compare(&self->iavctx->ch_layout,
+                                     &self->oavctx->ch_layout) != 0;
 }
 
 static int
